{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvzBgfRbAKfRZWpqnsBQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HhLVqyaLwcH89jDr1bTYw2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\np='paper.tex'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"Exact conditional coverage is impossible in general without further structure, which has motivated relaxations that target class-, group- or feature-conditional guarantees \\\\citep{Gibbs2023ConformalPW,Bairaktari2025KandinskyCP}.\"\nb=\"Several works address conditional-coverage guarantees beyond the marginal guarantee, including conditional guarantees for conformal prediction \\\\citep{Gibbs2023ConformalPW} and coverage beyond class- and covariate-conditional notions \\\\citep{Bairaktari2025KandinskyCP}.\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b)\na=\"H2 is addressed by the development comparison V1 versus V2 and by the sealed shift-case gap;\"\nb=\"H2 is supported only descriptively by the development comparison V1 versus V2 on three seeds, while the sealed shift-case gap is a residual of the frozen procedure with no unweighted or baseline counterpart and so does not test H2;\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b)\na=\"so part of its advantage on the slice axis reflects a match between method and metric by design; the class-wise baseline shares this alignment, but its individual score is not retained.\"\nb=\"so slice-axis results may partly reflect this alignment between method and metric; the class-wise baseline calibrates per label as well, and no per-axis baseline comparison is retained, so any slice-axis advantage is unmeasured.\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"Gibbs2023\\|Bairaktari\" claims_grounding.json | head; grep -n \"section{\\|subsection{\\|paragraph{\" paper.tex | head -60"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3426,"ca